This repository contains original work by the ruby-ios-bringup contributors and
references the following upstream projects.

XNU
  Apple's open-source kernel, xnu-8796. The patches in patches/ are
  modifications to XNU and remain under the Apple Public Source License 2.0.
  No XNU source tree is included.

ios-sweet (dipa-studio)
  The original iOS-on-Sweet project. No license file was present at the
  referenced commit; upstream code is not copied into this repository.
  The complete 0001-0079 patch files are not included; the 0010/0012 change is
  published separately in ci/baseline-changes.patch.

ios-topaz (MakrSas)
  A fork of ios-sweet targeting the Redmi Note 12 4G. No license file was
  present at the referenced commit; upstream code is not copied into this repository.

blacktop/darwin-xnu-build
  MIT-licensed XNU build harness used by the upstream CI.

TWRP (Team Win Recovery Project)
  GPLv2. No TWRP image is included.

Magisk
  GPLv3. No Magisk image is included.

Apple iPhone X iOS 16.7.16 userland / IPSW
  Not included. Users must obtain their own copy and comply with Apple's terms.

This project is not affiliated with Apple, Xiaomi, MediaTek, or any upstream
project. All trademarks belong to their respective owners.

Redistribution note: ci/baseline-changes.patch contains a small modification to
two upstream patch files (0010/0012); the upstream tree is fetched by the
recipe, not copied into this repository. CI fetches the 82-file baseline patch
set from a private content-addressed mirror; only its manifest root and the
disclosed 0010/0012 change are published. No complete upstream patch file is
redistributed in this repository. The upstream projects had no license file
at the pinned commits. Obtain permission before public redistribution or keep
the repository private. See LEGAL.md.
